Third-party code in ktx2_transcoder.wasm

ktx2_transcoder.wasm is a WebAssembly (wasm32-wasip1) build of the KTX2
transcoder of Binomial's basis_universal v2.50
(https://github.com/BinomialLLC/basis_universal; copyright Binomial LLC and
other contributors) with the single-file Zstandard decoder it ships
(zstd/zstddeclib.c; copyright Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates). It is
compiled from the unmodified basis_universal v2.50 sources plus the wrapper
tools/basisu-wasm/ktx2_wasi.cc by tools/basisu-wasm/build-basisu-wasm.sh,
which pins and checksums every input.

basis_universal is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Its
license file is LICENSE-basis_universal and its NOTICE file is
NOTICE-basis_universal, both in this directory, copied unchanged from the
v2.50 source tree. Zstandard is offered under the BSD license or the GPLv2,
at the user's option; the BSD license is chosen here. Its license file is
LICENSE-zstd in this directory, copied unchanged from zstd/LICENSE of the
v2.50 source tree.

The module also links parts of the wasi-sdk 34 sysroot, the same wasi-sdk
as internal/draco's module (wasi-libc at commit
2e6fb9d8ee0cdf9e431fbcabe8af3115de000a13, llvm-project at commit
895aa2c896ada719451be2e3673c83da8ddf1141). The link of the module
(wasm-ld --trace, same output checksum) takes these inputs from it:

- wasi-libc: crt1-reactor.o and 245 members of libc.a, from the musl part,
  the cloudlibc part, wasi-libc's own sources and dlmalloc. emmalloc and
  fts are not linked.
- LLVM: 4 members of libc++.a, 4 of libc++abi.a and 20 of the compiler-rt
  builtins (libclang_rt.builtins.a), plus code of the libc++ headers.

Their license files are those listed in internal/draco/NOTICE, in
internal/draco/licenses/ (wasi-libc and its parts: musl, cloudlibc,
dlmalloc; libc++, libc++abi and compiler-rt).

internal/basisu runs the module with wazero (github.com/tetratelabs/wazero,
Apache License, Version 2.0), a Go module dependency compiled into the
rodin3d-mcp binary; its license and NOTICE are in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt
with the other Go modules.
